{"parentUuid":"6d8be9cb-4edd-4a22-8750-39213f043c14","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L9nteM4Hj7peXU73BdwPuJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Hexaly LocalSolver core technology primal heuristic local search whitepaper 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"(PDF) LocalSolver 1.x: A black-box local-search solver for 0-1 programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220340267_LocalSolver_1x_A_black-box_local-search_solver_for_0-1_programming\"},{\"title\":\"Local Search - Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/algorithms/local-search\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver (LocalSolver 8.0 API)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/8_0/java/localsolver/LocalSolver.html?redirect\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/\"},{\"title\":\"LocalSolver (LocalSolver 6.0 API)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/6_0/java/localsolver/LocalSolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"Localsolver: localsolver.LocalSolver Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/5_5/csharp/classlocalsolver_1_1_local_solver.html\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly sponsors OR 2022\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/events/localsolver-sponsors-or-2022\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly | LinkedIn\",\"url\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/hexaly\"},{\"title\":\"Mathematical Programming Solver Based on Local Search | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/263405426_Mathematical_Programming_Solver_Based_on_Local_Search\"},{\"title\":\"Now we are Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/announcements/now-we-are-hexaly\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query about Hexaly LocalSolver's core technology, primal heuristics, and local search. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe \"LocalSolver\" name refers to the generic \"local search\" algorithms that originally made the difference with traditional Mixed-Integer Linear Programming (MILP) solvers when the company launched in 2012. Over the years, LocalSolver became a Global Optimization solver, combining many different algorithmic methods: spatial branch-and-bound, simplex methods, interior-point methods, augmented Lagrangian methods, automatic Dantzig-Wolfe reformulation, column and row generation, propagation methods, local search, direct search, population-based methods, and surrogate modeling techniques for black-box optimization.\n\n## Local Search Technology\n\nLocal search is a general optimization technique that iteratively improves a candidate solution by exploring nearby solutions in the search space. It is widely used for solving combinatorial optimization problems, especially when exact algorithms become computationally expensive.\n\nLocal search is widely used both as a standalone heuristic and as a component of hybrid optimization approaches. In modern solvers, it often complements exact methods by quickly generating high-quality feasible solutions. These solutions can improve bounds in Branch-and-Bound frameworks or guide more sophisticated search strategies.\n\n## Primal Heuristics\n\nPrimal heuristics guarantee that feasible, high-quality solutions are provided at an early stage of the solving process, and thus are essential to the success of mixed-integer programming (MIP). By helping prove optimality faster, they allow MIP technology to extend to a wide variety of applications in discrete optimization.\n\nThe search results did not contain a specific 2025 whitepaper on these topics. You may want to visit Hexaly's official website directly or contact them for the latest technical documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5d12a6ba-9f75-4f52-b934-4b323b8ceb8e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:48.219Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6d8be9cb-4edd-4a22-8750-39213f043c14","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ba5bebda-fdaa-40c3-be0b-59f12c64a236","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BmUH4isMZjNehHiGPwDCJ5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"modern tabu search survey 2025 self-adaptive intensification diversification\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A novel adaptive search strategy of intensification and diversification in tabu search | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/1279300/;jsessionid=72ko1wMRsmDsjTuA9Gzte7WJYx-I4_kfzcSm0Gy9c22q00oUzWEa!1915905931\"},{\"title\":\"Intensification and Diversification Strategies with Tabu Search: One-Machine Problem with Weighted Tardiness Objective | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/10720076_5\"},{\"title\":\"The Granular Tabu Search and Its Application to the Vehicle-Routing Problem | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.15.4.333.24890\"},{\"title\":\"A Metaheuristic Tabu Search Optimization Algorithm: Applications to Chemical and Environmental Processes | IntechOpen\",\"url\":\"https://www.intechopen.com/chapters/77046\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Multistart Tabu Search and Diversification Strategies for the Quadratic Assignment Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/224396129_Multistart_Tabu_Search_and_Diversification_Strategies_for_the_Quadratic_Assignment_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"Principles of Tabu Search FRED GLOVER, MANUEL LAGUNA\",\"url\":\"https://www.uv.es/~rmarti/paper/docs/ts1.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Intensification and diversification with elite tabu search solutions for the linear ordering problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S030505489800104X\"},{\"title\":\"23 Principles of Tabu Search Fred Glover University of Colorado Manuel Laguna\",\"url\":\"https://leeds-faculty.colorado.edu/glover/fred%20pubs/376%20-%20TS%20-%20Principles%20of%20Tabu%20Search%20-%20Glover,%20Laguna%20and%20Marti.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"TABU SEARCH* Fred Glovera Manuel Lagunab\",\"url\":\"https://opttek.com/sites/default/files/TS_for_Handbook_of_Combinatorial_Optimization_2nd_Edition_SFE_Updated5-23-12.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Tabu Search Algorithm (TSA): A Comprehensive Survey\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/341405739_Tabu_Search_Algorithm_TSA_A_Comprehensive_Survey\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here is what I found about modern tabu search with self-adaptive intensification and diversification strategies:\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nIntensification and diversification are two highly important components of tabu search. However, these two components are often in conflict, making it worthy to study how to harmonize this conflict.\n\n## Intensification and Diversification Strategies\n\nIntensification strategies are used to search potential areas in detail around areas found good in the past, generally employed based on long-term memory whose components are used to create neighbors for search intensification. \n\nIn contrast, diversification strategies are used to search the complete viable region, restricting the search from getting trapped in local optima, promoting probing of unvisited regions by creating solutions radically different from those searched earlier.\n\n## Self-Adaptive Approaches\n\nRecent developments include novel adaptive search strategies of intensification and diversification in tabu search proposed to improve solving quality and efficiency, with computational experiments showing the proposed approach is feasible and effective.\n\n## Advanced Methods\n\nIntensification strategies modify choice rules to encourage move combinations and solution features historically found good, while diversification strategies seek to incorporate new attributes and attribute combinations not previously included in solutions.\n\nPath relinking, an advanced strategy for integrating intensification and diversification, operates by starting from a high-quality solution and generating a path in the neighborhood space that leads toward other solutions in a subset of elite solutions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e8dbeab1-68b6-45c0-8ad9-63b62bc389c6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:49.342Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ba5bebda-fdaa-40c3-be0b-59f12c64a236","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5530500e-d516-46c5-95aa-14ecd34a388f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M6QwmSZPs9STRbat3DKs7H","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"variable neighborhood search VNS GVNS packing placement 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Survey on Variable Neighborhood Search for Sustainable Logistics\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/1999-4893/18/1/38\"},{\"title\":\"General variable neighborhood search for the capacitated single allocation hub maximal covering problem | TOP | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11750-024-00685-9\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial GVNS (General Variable Neighborhood Search) Optimization for Dynamic Garbage Collection\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/1999-4893/11/4/38\"},{\"title\":\"A reinforcement learning-Variable neighborhood search method for the capacitated Vehicle Routing Problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0957417422018309\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding Variable Neighborhood Search | HackerNoon\",\"url\":\"https://hackernoon.com/understanding-variable-neighborhood-search\"},{\"title\":\"Study of the General Variable Neighborhood Search (GVNS) algorithm and Variable Neighborhood Search (VNS) algorithm in CVRPTW - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2022AIPC.2639d0008F/abstract\"},{\"title\":\"FNS If one uses Variable Neighborhood Descent instead of simple local... | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Figure-4-FNS-If-one-uses-Variable-Neighborhood-Descent-instead-of-simple-local-search_fig1_225198396\"},{\"title\":\"A General VNS heuristic for the traveling salesman problem with time windows | Discrete Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1016/j.disopt.2010.04.002\"},{\"title\":\"A variable neighborhood search approach for solving a real-world hierarchical multi-echelon vehicle routing problem involving HCT vehicles | Computers and Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1016/j.cor.2024.106594\"},{\"title\":\"Variable Neighborhood Search | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/0-387-28356-0_8\"}]\n\nI've successfully performed a web search for your query about Variable Neighborhood Search (VNS) and General Variable Neighborhood Search (GVNS) related to packing and placement problems in 2024-2025. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Recent Research (2024-2025)\n\nA comprehensive survey on Variable Neighborhood Search for Sustainable Logistics was published in January 2025, which provides insights into current VNS applications. This study explores the use of VNS, a metaheuristic optimization method, in addressing sustainable logistics challenges.\n\n## GVNS Applications\n\nGVNS is one of the most widely used versions of VNS, and GVNS is explicitly mentioned in 213 works. GVNS is a VNS variant where the VND method is used as the improvement procedure.\n\n## Packing and Placement Applications\n\nVariable Neighborhood Search (VNS) offers powerful strategies for optimizing bin packing problems, including neighborhoods like Move-Item, Swap-Items, and MoveTwo-to-One. \n\n## Recent 2024 Studies\n\nA General Variable Neighborhood Search (GVNS) heuristic was designed and implemented for solving a Capacitated Single Allocation Hub Maximal Covering Problem in 2024, demonstrating GVNS's effectiveness for location-allocation type problems.\n\nThe search results show that VNS and GVNS continue to be active areas of research with applications in logistics, routing, packing, and placement optimization problems through 2024-2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4455be77-a0b4-4387-af3c-5dae264c2bed","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:49.587Z","sourceTo