{"parentUuid":"a261deb6-cca5-4b0d-8ee8-28ed40482af7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SQaJw14DwfnXJXfyZkjAhJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Hexaly free academic license trial python API\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Installation on Windows — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/installation/installationonwindows.html\"},{\"title\":\"Download\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/download\"},{\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"Installation on Linux — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/installation/installationonlinux.html\"},{\"title\":\"Installation on Windows — Hexaly 14.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/installation/installationonwindows.html?redirect\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy Hexaly interface (cpmpy.solvers.hexaly) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/solver_modulenotfound/api/solvers/hexaly.html\"},{\"title\":\"Installation on macOS — Hexaly 14.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/installation/installationonmacosx.html\"},{\"title\":\"Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Installation on Linux — Hexaly 14.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/docs/last/installation/installationonlinux.html?redirect\"},{\"title\":\"Now we are Hexaly\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/announcements/now-we-are-hexaly\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Hexaly's free academic license, trial, and Python API:\n\n## Free Academic License and Trial\n\nTo get a free academic license or trial license, you need to register on the Hexaly website. Trial licenses offer the full features of the commercial version but are limited to 1-month. For academics, academic licenses are free for educational and fundamental research purposes, offering 3-month licenses that are renewable forever to individual students.\n\nAs licenses are manually delivered by a member of the Hexaly team, the whole procedure can take a few days to complete (usually 1 day).\n\n## Python API Support\n\nHexaly Optimizer can be used as a callable library including Python. For the Python library, Python >= 3.6 is required. \n\nFor Python installation details, the 'hexaly' python package can be installed with: pip install hexaly -i https://pip.hexaly.com.\n\nThe official Hexaly Python API documentation is available in their official documentation, which you can access through their installation guides on the Hexaly website.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"50a4b379-4974-451e-8b39-f4595684c4e1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:00.927Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a261deb6-cca5-4b0d-8ee8-28ed40482af7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e608ad9d-e658-4eec-b04e-4e8f455111b7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GHyapBDc23aqzzpKS2QFG4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"VLSI floorplan simulated annealing tabu search 2D placement metaheuristic\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"IC Floorplanning Optimization using Simulated Annealing ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.mecs-press.org/ijisa/ijisa-v13-n2/IJISA-V13-N2-5.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"On Using Tabu Search for Design Automation of VLSI Systems | Journal of Heuristics | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1023/A:1021893712145.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) SIMULATED ANNEALING ALGORITHM FOR MODERN VLSI FLOORPLANNING PROBLEM\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/306363254_SIMULATED_ANNEALING_ALGORITHM_FOR_MODERN_VLSI_FLOORPLANNING_PROBLEM\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Hybrid Simulated Annealing Algorithm for Nonslicing VLSI Floorplanning\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/224174253_A_Hybrid_Simulated_Annealing_Algorithm_for_Nonslicing_VLSI_Floorplanning\"},{\"title\":\"Simulated Annealing Algorithm for VLSI Floorplanning for Soft Blocks | PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/simulated-annealing-algorithm-for-vlsi-floorplanning-for-soft-blocks/96418415\"},{\"title\":\"A fast force-directed simulated annealing for 3D IC partitioning | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/304025765_A_fast_force-directed_simulated_annealing_for_3D_IC_partitioning\"},{\"title\":\"Non Slicing floorplan Representations in VLSI ...\",\"url\":\"https://research.ijcaonline.org/volume71/number15/pxc3888962.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Simulated annealing for VLSI design: | Guide books | ACM Digital Library\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.5555/53631\"},{\"title\":\"An Efficient Simulated Annealing Based VLSI Floorplanning Algorithm for Slicing Structure | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/6394327/\"},{\"title\":\"Floorplanning / Simulated Annealing – CADApps – Visualizations of VLSI CAD\",\"url\":\"https://sites.lafayette.edu/cadapps/main-page/floorplanning-simulated-annealing/\"}]\n\nI've successfully retrieved search results for your query on VLSI floorplanning using simulated annealing, tabu search, and 2D placement metaheuristics. Here's a summary of the key findings:\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nIC floorplanning is an NP-hard problem with no polynomial time exact algorithm for quick solution in reasonable time. Floorplanning is defined as the process of placing circuit blocks to a given 2D boundary, with constraints that all blocks should be kept into a given 2D boundary and there is no overlap between any two blocks.\n\n## Simulated Annealing Approach\n\nSimulated Annealing is a general approach to optimization in which small transformations called moves are randomly applied to a configuration, where moves that decrease cost are always accepted, while moves that increase cost are accepted probabilistically under control of a temperature parameter.\n\nA Simulated Spheroidizing Annealing Algorithm (SSAA) has been developed with improvements suggested to enhance performance.\n\n## Tabu Search Application\n\nTabu search is a meta-heuristic problem solving technique that, when applied carefully, provides near optimal solutions in a very short time.\n\n## Hybrid Approaches\n\nResearchers have combined ideas from simulated annealing into two-staged tabu search and proposed hybrid algorithms, with simulated annealing embedded into tabu search for floorplanning.\n\nThe iterative methods use metaheuristic strategies, such as simulated annealing, genetic algorithm, and tabu search, to produce good solutions.\n\nThe search results contain extensive academic literature on these optimization techniques applied to VLSI floorplanning problems, with implementations tested on standard benchmarks like MCNC (Microelectronics Centre of North Carolina).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"76a27f2d-3b49-471e-9b87-fb2bfc060fb7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:01.098Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e608ad9d-e658-4eec-b04e-4e8f455111b7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e202d14f-fbf4-45d5-a8a9-01befda9cb8e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F1ZFQq72FE1XCu1qqxtFHL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT AddHint warm start incumbent OR-Tools best practice\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/cp_optimizer/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"What does exactly AddHint method do? · google/or-tools · Discussion #3277\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3277\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"warm start cp-sat ortools\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/minizinc/c/1QRwbQhStHg\"},{\"title\":\"📈 #76 Optimizing with Google OR-Tools: strategies and insights from three years of real-world experience\",\"url\":\"https://www.feasible.club/p/76-optimizing-with-google-or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/model.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/model.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CP-SAT AddHint warm start and best practices:\n\n## How AddHint Works\n\nA solution hint is not a hard constraint. The solver will try to use it in search for a while, and then gradually revert to its default search technique. OR-Tools supports warmstarting the solver with a feasible solution. More specifically, it will branch that variable on that value first if possible. This is known as 'phase saving' in the SAT literature, but then extended to integer variables.\n\n## Best Practices\n\n**Complete Hints Preferred:** CP-SAT prefers full hints, meaning all variables.\n\n**Key Constraints on Hints:** Hints must cover all variables they touch and remain feasible after presolve or they're ignored silently. So if the solver finds no feasible solutions, your hint was inconsistent.\n\n**Flexibility with Partial Hints:** Despite the preference for full hints, solution hints don't need to use all variables: partial solution hints are fine. Additionally, it's OK to have an infeasible solution hint. It can still be helpful in some repair procedures, where one wants to identify a solution close to a previously violated state.\n\n**Performance Benefit:** The solution hint does NOT need to satisfy all constraints, it should just provide reasonable default values for the variables. Warm-starting is an optimization where the solver uses the previous solution as a starting point or \"hint\" for the next iteration. This technique can significantly speed up the solving process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6bada2ef-68a8-496e-b1e6-de98bf4252a7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:01.574Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e202d14f-fbf4-45d5-a8a9-01befda9cb8e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f8ad24e4-6c81-4423-b41a-434b41a5b34f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WihvnaQRMxw9ZWN4fHKT9v","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"hyper-heuristic adaptive operator selection combinatorial optimization 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"HeurAgenix: A Multi-Agent LLM-Based Paradigm for Adaptive Heuristic Evolution and Selection in Combinatorial Optimization | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=xxSK3ZNAhh\"},{\"title\":\"Nature Index Hyper-Heuristic Approaches for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/nature-index/topics/l4/hyper-heuristic-approaches-for-combinatorial-optimization\"},{\"title\":\"HeurAgenix: Leveraging LLMs for Solving Complex Combinatorial Optimization Challenges\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.15196v1\"},{\"title\":\"Automated Hyper-Heuristic Evolution and Dynamic Selection in Complex Combinatorial Optimization Through Contrastive Learning and Dual-Reward Mechanisms | by ~ | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@advancedsoftwareengineering/automated-hyper-heuristic-evolution-and-dynamic-selection-in-complex-combinatorial-optimization-7a3cda6fbe69\"},{\"title\":\"Hyper-heuristic Operator Selection and Acceptance Criteria | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/294278098_Hyper-heuristic_Operator_Selection_and_Acceptance_Criteria\"},{\"title\":\"A hyper-heuristic approach based on adaptive selection operator and behavioral schema for global optimization | Soft Computing - A Fusion of Foundations, Methodologies and Applications\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1007/s00500-023-09018-7\"},{\"title\":\"A hyper-heuristic approach based on adaptive selection operator and behavioral schema for global optimization | Soft Computing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00500-023-09018-7\"},{\"title\":\"Hyper-heuristics | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-3-032-00385-0_32\"},{\"title\":\"A hyper-heuristic approach based on adaptive selection operator and behavioral schema for global optimization | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/372988784_A_hyper-heuristic_approach_based_on_adaptive_selection_operator_and_behavioral_schema_for_global_optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Full article: Adaptive operator selection in heuristic optimization utilizing generalized experience with reinforcement learning\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/17445760.2025.2605297\"}]\n\nHere are the search results for \"hyper-heuristic adaptive operator selection combinatorial optimization 2024 2025\":\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Recent Developments (2024-2025)\n\nHeurAgenix is a novel multi-agent hyper-heuristic framework that leverages LLMs to generate, evolve, evaluate, and select heuristics for solving CO problems. This framework was submitted to ICLR 2025 and represents cutting-edge work in this space.\n\nHeurAgenix addresses limitations by introducing a unified framework for automatic heuristic evolution and adaptive selection, and is the first LLM-based hyper-heuristic framework that simultaneously evolves a diverse pool of heuristics without relying on any external solver and incorporates an online heuristic selector for adaptive problem solving.\n\n### Core Concepts\n\nA hyper-heuristic is a high-level method that selects, generates or adapts heuristics to solve optimisation problems broadly, with selection hyper-heuristics representing a variant that chooses one of several predefined low-level heuristics at each iteration.\n\nTwo main paradigms have emerged: selection hyper-heuristics, which choose from predefined heuristics at each step, and generation hyper-heuristics, which construct novel heuristics from components, with recent advances incorporating machine learning to capture search behaviour and transfer knowledge between problem domains.\n\n### Latest 2025 Research\n\nThe growing trend of employing multiple operators with adaptive operator selection schemes aims to address exploration-exploitation issues, though there remains a significant demand for utilizing tailored adaptive selection schemes in search.\n\nThe search results show active ongoing research in this field with applications to combinatorial optimization problems including vehicle routing, timetabling, and scheduling.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a59f79b6-e90c-4b91-b9d8-a62959ee45ee","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:02.108Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f8ad24e4-6c81-4423-b41a-434b41a5b34f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
