{"parentUuid":"8efb25e9-2d67-4631-81eb-10eee9ea7690","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013EBmdYEwPoaiPMumAF71gU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q3fDg9pywcY6kLAN5XUhQN","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"2D rectangle packing\" tabu search ALNS metaheuristic benchmark"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5037,"cache_read_input_tokens":31772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5037,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":42,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caotr6hoTKatbDNzbcNUk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"864d72f4-dd39-4c38-89dc-d650b6329958","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:22.462Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"864d72f4-dd39-4c38-89dc-d650b6329958","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013EBmdYEwPoaiPMumAF71gU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0187w6WxqYZkBj24awmGeBUn","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"facility layout problem tabu search 2024 simulated annealing comparison"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5037,"cache_read_input_tokens":31772,"output_tokens":323,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5037},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":31772,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5037,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caotr6hoTKatbDNzbcNUk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"98cfc992-59b8-4dad-b0e9-2af413c59515","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:22.810Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8efb25e9-2d67-4631-81eb-10eee9ea7690","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LjP589AzedZWUvrGi2EXBW","type":"tool_result","content":"# Using External Solutions with CP-SAT LNS\n\nBased on the provided content, **the document does not contain information about using external incumbent solutions, AddHint best practices, or combining externally generated heuristic solutions with CP-SAT's LNS functionality**.\n\nThe primer focuses on:\n- How LNS works conceptually (destroy and repair)\n- Example implementations for knapsack and TSP problems\n- Strategy selection methods (exploration vs. exploitation)\n\n## What the Content Does Cover\n\nThe material explains that you can leverage domain knowledge to enhance LNS performance: \"You on the other hand know a lot about your problem and can use this knowledge to implement a more efficient version.\" However, this refers to designing better neighborhood selection strategies—not specifically to seeding CP-SAT with external solutions.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nTo answer your question accurately, you would need to consult:\n- Official Google OR-Tools CP-SAT documentation on the `AddHint()` method\n- Code examples in the referenced notebook: `examples/lns_knapsack.ipynb`\n- Additional resources beyond this primer\n\nThe primer establishes LNS principles but doesn't address the specific API mechanics for combining external heuristic solutions with CP-SAT."}]},"uuid":"7c310ccc-aed0-4c29-acfa-29534445f1ae","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:26.204Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8efb25e9-2d67-4631-81eb-10eee9ea7690","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"98cfc992-59b8-4dad-b0e9-2af413c59515","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0187w6WxqYZkBj24awmGeBUn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"facility layout problem tabu search 2024 simulated annealing comparison\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"An empirical comparison of tabu search, simulated annealing, and genetic algorithms for facilities location problems | Guide books\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.5555/925705\"},{\"title\":\"An empirical comparison of Tabu Search, Simulated Annealing, and Genetic Algorithms for facilities location problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0925527306000971\"},{\"title\":\"An empirical comparison of Tabu Search, Simulated ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.bauer.uh.edu/doctoral/scm/docs/Khumawala-2006.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A new hybrid tabu-simulated annealing heuristic for the dynamic facility layout problem: International Journal of Production Research: Vol 47, No 24\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/00207540802376323?tab=permissions&scroll=top\"},{\"title\":\"Intelligent local search strategies for solving facility layout problems with the quadratic assignment problem formulation - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221797002853\"},{\"title\":\"Simulated Annealing and Genetic Algorithms for the Facility Layout Problem: A Survey | Computational Optimization and Applications | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1023/A:1008623913524\"},{\"title\":\"A new hybrid tabu-simulated annealing heuristic for the dynamic facility layout problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/232994825_A_new_hybrid_tabu-simulated_annealing_heuristic_for_the_dynamic_facility_layout_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Comparative performance of tabu search and simulated annealing heuristics for the quadratic assignment problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0167637710001264\"},{\"title\":\"Simulated annealing and tabu search approaches for the Corridor Allocation Problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221713005808\"},{\"title\":\"An improved tabu search heuristic for solving facility layout design problems: International Journal of Production Research: Vol 34, No 9\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/00207549608905045\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive research on facility layout problems using tabu search and simulated annealing. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overall Performance Comparison\n\nTabu search tends to give the most robust results closely followed by simulated annealing. When comparing the relative performance of Tabu Search, Simulated Annealing, and Genetic Algorithms on various types of facility location problems, Tabu Search shows very good performance in most cases.\n\n## Context-Dependent Results\n\nThe relative effectiveness of these algorithms can depend on specific conditions:\n\n- When all heuristics are limited to the same amount of computation time, tabu search performs consistently well for all three problem types.\n- For some facility location problem variants, the performance of simulated annealing shows no statistically significant difference from tabu search.\n- For a number of varied problem instances, Simulated Annealing performs better for higher quality targets while Tabu Search performs better for lower quality targets.\n\n## Hybrid Approaches\n\nResearch has also explored combining both methods: The hybrid tabu search heuristic, combining the advantages from both tabu search and simulated annealing, can generally outperform their parent algorithms.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nTabu Search should be tried first to the extent that it always yields as good or better results and is easy to develop and implement.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cd86edbf-eec0-4838-bec1-bae6a4bc678a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:29.446Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"98cfc992-59b8-4dad-b0e9-2af413c59515","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"864d72f4-dd39-4c38-89dc-d650b6329958","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q3fDg9pywcY6kLAN5XUhQN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"2D rectangle packing\" tabu search ALNS metaheuristic benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Reinforced Tabu Search Approach for 2D Strip Packing | IGI Global Scientific Publishing\",\"url\":\"https://www.igi-global.com/gateway/article/47373\"},{\"title\":\"Metaheuristic Algorithms for the Strip Packing Problem | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-1-4613-0233-9_7\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - itsatefe/Metaheuristic-Algorithms: Metaheuristic Algorithms for Bin Packing Problem (1D and 2D)\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/itsatefe/Metaheuristic-Algorithms\"},{\"title\":\"An improved skyline based heuristic for the 2D strip packing problem and its efficient implementation - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054816302982\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive large neighborhood search for solving the circle bin packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054820302574\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Skyline-Based Heuristic for the 2D Rectangular Strip Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221049934_A_Skyline-Based_Heuristic_for_the_2D_Rectangular_Strip_Packing_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"TSpack: A Unified Tabu Search Code for Multi-Dimensional Bin Packing Problems | Annals of Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1023/B:ANOR.0000039519.03572.08\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A REVIEW META- HEURISTIC APPROACHES FOR SOLVING RECTANGLE PACKING PROBLEM\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/4753130/A_REVIEW_META_HEURISTIC_APPROACHES_FOR_SOLVING_RECTANGLE_PACKING_PROBLEM\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) TSpack: A Unified Tabu Search Code for Multi-Dimensional Bin Packing Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/44707057_TSpack_A_Unified_Tabu_Search_Code_for_Multi-Dimensional_Bin_Packing_Problems\"},{\"title\":\"Heuristic and metaheuristic approaches for a class of two-dimensional bin packing problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/1152541/Heuristic_and_metaheuristic_approaches_for_a_class_of_two_dimensional_bin_packing_problems\"}]\n\nI've completed a web search for \"2D rectangle packing tabu search ALNS metaheuristic benchmark\". Here are the key findings:\n\n## Tabu Search for 2D Rectangle Packing\n\nA reinforced tabu search approach has been presented for 2D strip packing, with two important components of the tabu search strategy reinforced to include problem knowledge. This approach was evaluated on a set of well-known hard benchmark instances and compared with state-of-the-art algorithms.\n\nTSpack is a computer code that implements a general Tabu Search technique for the solution of two- and three-dimensional bin packing problems.\n\n## ALNS (Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search) for 2D Packing\n\nAn adaptive large neighborhood search (ALNS) heuristic has been specifically designed for handling large instances of 2D packing problems. The ALNS incorporates eleven removal operators and seven insertion operators, offering a comprehensive exploration and improvement of solutions.\n\nThese algorithms were compared with a representative sample of metaheuristics from the literature in terms of solution quality on a large set of 1,718 benchmark instances, and the new algorithms compared favorably with, and in some cases outperformed, existing strip packing metaheuristics.\n\n## Hybrid Approaches\n\nA tailored adaptive large neighborhood search (TALNS) algorithm has been proposed, combining the adaptive large neighborhood search algorithm and the tabu search heuristic in a single framework.\n\nThe search results demonstrate active research combining both tabu search and ALNS metaheuristics for 2D rectangle packing problems with extensive benchmarking on standard test instances.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e7e80854-2be8-4ea5-a754-531dfcbef920","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:29.579Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"864d72f4-dd39-4c38-89dc-d650b6329958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e7e80854-2be8-4ea5-a754-531dfcbef920","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7322ed66982214c7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Qrcm11FDvV1Ebg8zZE5Ygu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"我已经收集了足够的信息。下面汇总输出。\n\n---\n\n## 调研报告：现代启发式工业求解器 — 作为 exploratory 加速器的可行性\n\n### 1. 核心算法横向对比\n\n| 方法 | 适合 70x70 placement | 工程量 | 与 CP-SAT 协同 | 主要风险 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **ALNS** (Adaptive LNS) | 高（destroy/repair 适合 packing） | 中（有成熟 Python 库 `alns`） | 直接产 incumbent 给 AddHint | 算子设计是关键 |\n| **Tabu Search** | 高（QAP/facility layout 经典领域） | 中（需自写 tabu list + aspiration） | 同上 | tabu list 调参敏感 |\n| **VNS / GVNS** | 中-高（多邻域结构对 packing 友好） | 低-中（结构简单） | 同上 | 单线程，扩展性一般 |\n| **Hexaly (LocalSolver)** | 黑盒、可能很强 | 低（声明式建模） | 不开源、不能交 hint 进 CP-SAT | 商业、3 个月学术 license |\n| **VLSI 风格 SA** | 高（floorplan 同源问题） | 中 | 标准 incumbent 输出 | 退火参数调优费时 |\n| **Hyper-heuristic / RL 控制** | 中 | 高（需训练或调权重） | 同 ALNS | 过工程化，对 266 实例不一定划算 |\n\n### 2. 核心技术要点\n\n**Hexaly (LocalSolver)：** 公开资料里没有详细算法说明，强调\"primal-heuristic-first + 局部搜索\"+ multi-start，组合了 spatial branch-and-bound、Dantzig-Wolfe、列生成、population-based、surrogate modeling。**关键限制：闭源，无法把它生成的解通过 API 取出来 hint 进 CP-SAT**（学术 license 3 个月可续，但耦合到 production 风险高）。借鉴价值在于\"声明式建模 + 多算法投票\"思路，不是直接拿来用。\n\n**现代 Tabu Search：** Glover 经典框架仍是基础。SOTA 加成主要是：(1) **adaptive tabu tenure**（动态调整禁忌长度）、(2) **path relinking** 做 intensification、(3) **frequency-based long-term memory** 做 diversification、(4) **granular tabu search**（限制邻域规模）。在 facility layout / QAP 类问题上，tabu 通常和 SA 并列第一档（\"tabu 在低质量区更稳，SA 在高质量区更细\"）。\n\n**VNS / GVNS：** 优势是多邻域结构对 packing 类天然契合（Move-Item / Swap-Items / MoveTwo-to-One 都是现成 move）。GVNS = VNS + VND（变邻域下降）做 local search。**与 LNS 的本质区别**：LNS 是 destroy 一大块再修复（破坏邻域规模大），VNS 是按规模递增遍历多个邻域结构（破坏小但形态多）。两者可叠加。\n\n**VLSI floorplan 借鉴：** B*-tree / sequence-pair 表示 + SA 的 perturb（rotate / swap / move）几十年的成熟范式，70x70 grid placement 完全可以借用 swap/move/rotate 的 move 集合。\n\n### 3. 关键开源库\n\n- **`alns` (N-Wouda/ALNS)** — Python，JOSS 发表，文档齐全，自带 RouletteWheel/SegmentedRouletteWheel 算子选择、HillClimbing/SimulatedAnnealing/RecordToRecordTravel 接受准则。**首推。**\n- **alberto-santini/adaptive-large-neighbourhood-search** — C++ header-only，性能更高但要写 binding。\n- **DR-ALNS (ICAPS 2024)** — RL 控制 ALNS 算子选择，研究价值高但工程化重。\n- **Tabu / VNS** Python 库零散，建议**自写**（200-400 行就够），参考 `mlrose` / `metaheuristics` 框架。\n- **Hexaly Python**：`pip install hexaly -i https://pip.hexaly.com`，3 个月学术许可，仅做对比基准，不进 production。\n\n### 4. CP-SAT AddHint 注意事项\n\n- **完整 hint 优先**，部分 hint 可用但效果弱；\n- hint 必须**在 presolve 后仍可行**，否则被静默丢弃；\n- 可以是不可行解（用于 repair），但效果不如可行解；\n- CP-SAT 的 LNS workers 已内置 RINS 风格策略，外部 incumbent 主要用于**给 master CP-SAT 一个好的初始 upper bound**，缩短证明时间。\n\n### 5. 对 exploratory 路径的具体建议\n\n**推荐栈：ALNS (alns lib) + Tabu 元素 + VLSI 风格 move 集合，输出 incumbent → CP-SAT AddHint。**\n\n具体方案：\n\n1. **第一阶段 (1-2 天)**：用 `alns` 库搭一个最小可跑版本：\n   - state = 266 实例的 (x,y,rotation) 列表 + ghost rectangle 位置\n   - destroy: random_remove (k=10-30)、worst_density_remove、spatial_cluster_remove\n   - repair: bottom-left-fill、greedy_largest_first、skyline_repair（VLSI 同源算法）\n   - 接受准则：`SimulatedAnnealing(start_temp=10, end_temp=0.1, step=0.95)`\n   - 算子选择：`SegmentedRouletteWheel` + 4 档 reward (best / better / accepted / rejected)\n\n2. **第二阶段 (1 天)**：加 tabu 元素 — 维护最近 K 步的 (instance_id, position) 禁忌表，禁止逆操作；加 `aspiration_criterion`（破纪录无视禁忌）。\n\n3. **第三阶段 (0.5 天)**：把最佳 incumbent 转换成 CP-SAT 变量赋值，调 `model.AddHint(var, val)`，跟现有 RINS warm-start 并存。\n\n4. **跟 Round 2 RINS 的关系**：**叠加，不是替代**。RINS 是 CP-SAT 内部从 LP relaxation 派生邻域，外部 ALNS 是从**结构化 placement 知识**派生 incumbent，两者信息源不同。最佳实践是 ALNS 先跑 60-120s 出 incumbent，再交给 CP-SAT 启动 + RINS 自动接管。\n\n5. **Hexaly**：建议**不上 production**，但值得申请学术 license，**只用作 exploratory benchmark**——拿 70x70 跑一次看它的 best-known incumbent 比我们 ALNS 强多少，作为天花板参考。\n\n**预期收益：** Hexaly 类启发式的核心优势在\"30 秒内拿到能用的解\"。对我们 168h 的精确 campaign，前 1-2% 时间投入 ALNS 通常能让 CP-SAT 早期就有紧的 upper bound，**经验值是缩短证明时间 20-50%**（packing 问题上 RINS + 好 hint 的典型加速）。\n\n**红线确认：** ALNS/Tabu 输出仅作为 hint，**绝不写入 `data/checkpoints/` 或当作 proof 来源**，符合 PROJECT_LOCK 的 exact/exploratory 隔离原则。\n\n---\n\nSources:\n- [Hexaly Local Search](https://www.hexaly.com/algorithms/local-search)\n- [Hexaly Pricing & Academic License](https://www.hexaly.com/pricing)\n- [LocalSolver 1.x black-box local-search 论文](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220340267_LocalSolver_1x_A_black-box_local-search_solver_for_0-1_programming)\n- [Principles of Tabu Search - Glover & Laguna](https://www.uv.es/~rmarti/paper/docs/ts1.pdf)\n- [Tabu Search Algorithm: A Comprehensive Survey](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/341405739_Tabu_Search_Algorithm_TSA_A_Comprehensive_Survey)\n- [VNS for Sustainable Logistics Survey 2025](https://www.mdpi.com/1999-4893/18/1/38)\n- [N-Wouda/ALNS Python library](https://github.com/N-Wouda/ALNS)\n- [ALNS JOSS paper](https://www.theoj.org/joss-papers/joss.05028/10.21105.joss.05028.pdf)\n- [DR-ALNS ICAPS 2024](https://github.com/RobbertReijnen/DR-ALNS)\n- [CP-SAT Primer - LNS](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html)\n- [CP-SAT AddHint discussion](https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3277)\n- [RINS original paper - Danna et al.](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-004-0518-7)\n- [Adaptive LNS for MIP](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12532-021-00209-7)\n- [Reinforced Tabu Search for 2D Strip Packing](https://www.igi-global.com/gateway/article/47373)\n- [TSpack - Tabu Search for bin packing](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1023/B:ANOR.0000039519.03572.08)\n- [ALNS for circle bin packing](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054820302574)\n- [Tabu Search for VLSI Design](https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1023/A:1021893712145.pdf)\n- [SA for VLSI Floorplanning](https://www.mecs-press.org/ijisa/ijisa-v13-n2/IJISA-V13-N2-5.pdf)\n- [HeurAgenix - LLM hyper-heuristic ICLR 2025](https://openreview.net/forum?id=xxSK3ZNAhh)\n- [Hybrid tabu-SA for dynamic facility layout](https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/00207540802376323)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1378,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2341,"cache_read_input_tokens":36809,"output_tokens":3637,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2341},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1378,"output_tokens":3637,"cache_read_input_tokens":36809,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2341,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotrydRuSbFqiZXcwtLM","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"382173eb-e2c2-41ce-8b5f-7db60d32cf59","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:35.619Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
